Saves stay in memory, and the Saturn tells the frontend where they are.

Mednafen writes the Saturn's backup memory, a cartridge's and the clock
chip's to files a few seconds after the game changes them, and again when
the game is closed; and when a game starts it puts a copy of each save file
aside. In Chimera a save is part of the machine: it lives in the machine's
memory, where a savestate holds it and going back in time takes it back
too, and the user writes it to a file with Export Save Data. A project's
save data is a file that is read and never written.

So the Saturn's three save functions do nothing, no copies of save files
are made (any system), and the Saturn says where its backup memories are
(MDFN_ChimeraSaveMemory). Loading is untouched: a project that starts from
a saved game gives Mednafen the file to read.

